(destination_availability_confirmed destination_availability_alpha) - currently? We have destination_availability_alpha candidate_created, but not confirmed. Need to confirm.

(destination_availability_locked destination_availability_alpha) - need to lock.

(destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha) - need to occupy destination node.

(destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha) - need to ready destination node.

(dispatch_allocated destination_availability_alpha) - need to allocate dispatch slot to destination_availability_alpha (but also candidate_dispatch_slot_linked needed). Actually dispatch_allocated predicate is separate from candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. For destination_availability_alpha, we need dispatch_allocated true.

(dispatch_allocated origin_availability_alpha) - need dispatch_allocated true.

(dispatch_ready destination_availability_alpha) - need dispatch_ready true.

(dispatch_ready origin_availability_alpha) - need dispatch_ready true.

(dispatched origin_availability_alpha) - need dispatched true.

(dispatched shift_candidate_alpha) - already dispatched? Not in init; we have dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true, but dispatched? Not listed. So need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha.

(origin_availability_confirmed origin_availability_alpha) - need to confirm.

(origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha) - need to lock.

