(transport_leg_destination_linked transport_leg_alpha destination_node_alpha) - need after assemble.

(transport_leg_loading_authorized transport_leg_alpha) - need to authorize.

(transport_leg_origin_linked transport_leg_alpha origin_node_alpha) - after assemble.

(vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta) - need to allocate vehicle to shift_candidate_beta.

(vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha) - currently vehicle_unit_alpha is allocated to origin_availability_alpha (candidate_vehicle_linked origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha) and vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha true, so vehicle_unit_alpha is not available. Need to release it (maybe deallocate? There's no explicit deallocate action; but vehicle_allocated is only set true by allocate_vehicle_unit; there is no action to unset vehicle_allocated. However vehicle_available predicate can be made true by certain actions: execute_*_dispatch actions have effect (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit). Also allocate_vehicle_unit has effect (not (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit)). So to make vehicle_available again, we need to execute a dispatch action that consumes the vehicle? Actually execute_origin_dispatch etc have effect (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) and (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot). They also set (dispatched ?candidate). So we can dispatch the origin_availability_alpha (or destination) to free the vehicle.

Thus we need to dispatch origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha and shift_candidate_alpha to free vehicles and dispatch slots.

Goal also expects vehicle_available vehicle_unit_alpha after all actions.

We need to produce minimal plan.

We have many actions available.

We need to prepare destination_availability_alpha and origin_availability_alpha and shift_candidate_beta.

Preparation involves: candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, candidate_task_profile_linked, then confirm_candidate_preparedness.

