h_slot_alpha true, and dispatch_slot_available false. If we later allocate to destination, we need dispatch_slot_available true (which is false). So cannot. However after we dispatch origin via execute_origin_dispatch, effect includes dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot (makes it available again) but does not remove candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot. So after dispatching origin, we would have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked origin dispatch_slot_alpha still true, and dispatch_slot_available true. Then we can allocate to destination, resulting in both origin and destination having candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true, and dispatch_slot_available false after allocation. That satisfies goal: both linked to same slot, slot not available. Good.

